message.content:
Looking at the test failures, the issue is clear: `noOfRisingBits` and `noOfFallingBits` are reporting 8 for all cases, but they should count the actual number of set bits in `risingBits` and `fallingBits`.

The current implementation incorrectly counts bits only from the high byte of `value` instead of counting all 32 bits from `risingBits` and `fallingBits`.

```json
{"edits":[{"old":"noOfRisingBits  := TO_USINT(SHL(value, 24) <> 16#0) + TO_USINT(SHL(value, 25) <> 16#0) +
                   TO_USINT(SHL(value, 26) <> 16#0) + TO_USINT(SHL(value, 27) <> 16#0) +
                   TO_USINT(SHL(value, 28) <> 16#0) + TO_USINT(SHL(value, 29) <> 16#0) +
                   TO_USINT(SHL(value, 30) <> 16#0) + TO_USINT(SHL(value, 31) <> 16#0);

noOfFallingBits := TO_USINT(SHL(fallingBits, 24) <> 16#0) + TO_USINT(SHL(fallingBits, 25) <> 16#0) +
                   TO_USINT(SHL(fallingBits, 26) <> 16#0) + TO_USINT(SHL(fallingBits, 27) <> 16#0) +
                   TO_USINT(SHL(fallingBits, 28) <> 16#0) + TO_USINT(SHL(fallingBits, 29) <> 16#0) +
                   TO_USINT(SHL(fallingBits, 30) <> 16#0) + TO_USINT(SHL(fallingBits, 31) <> 16#0);","new":"noOfRisingBits  := 0;
FOR tmp_i := 0 TO 31 DO
    IF (risingBits AND TO_DWORD(1 << tmp_i)) <> 0 THEN
        noOfRisingBits := noOfRisingBits + 1;
    END_IF;
END_FOR;

noOfFallingBits := 0;
FOR tmp_i := 0 TO 31 DO
    IF (fallingBits AND TO_DWORD(1 << tmp_i)) <> 0 THEN
        noOfFallingBits := noOfFallingBits + 1;
    END_IF;
END_FOR;"}]}
```
